## Old-school Based
Using paper and forms to organise meetings/appiontments would be feasible for a small scale school but it is high illadvisbale to impliment it into a college-level enviroment.
It could operate find for in-society meetings, but the society officer(s) would likely generate a headache trying to keep a plethora of papers and folders contains sensitive inforamtion organised and safe.

There is also the added con of privacy, a sheet of paper posted on a notice board,  similar to a sign-up chart, is public and may 'out' a student who does not wish for their appiontment to be made public.

## Email Based
A system designed around Stakeholders send emails to arrange appiontments would be preferable for a middle-populated college, rather than eiter of the suggested solutions proposed above.
This system however would grant resonsibility to the ones arranging meetings, such as receptionists and their superior.

While it is a receptionists job to arganise meetings and such - a college would typically have hundreds of students looking for appiontments and this may very well be overwhelming.

A possible solution is teaching students the correct format for arranging an email - while also allowing the superior (such as a DSS Officer) to arrange the meetings themselves while the receptionist simply verifies and forwards.
This method would also disable any spam/scam or innapropirate emails (Innapropirate being emails to; arrange a meeting with person A but emailing person H or sending emails without the correct format).
